  <h1>Seat Sherpa vs Amtrak in California</h1>
  <div class="meta">Updated September 2026 · Prices are typical ranges; live seat prices are on each route page</div>

  <p class="lede"><strong>Short answer:</strong> it depends on the corridor. Where Amtrak runs a direct train, such as Los Angeles to San Diego on the Pacific Surfliner or Sacramento to the Bay Area on the Capitol Corridor, the train is a strong option and a carpool mainly wins on price and door-to-door time. Where there is no direct train, which includes San Francisco to Los Angeles and Los Angeles to Las Vegas, a Seat Sherpa carpool seat is both cheaper and hours faster.</p>

  <h2>Corridor by corridor</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table class="stack">
    <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Amtrak</th><th>Seat Sherpa seat</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>San Francisco to Los Angeles</td><td data-l="Amtrak">No direct train. San Joaquins plus Thruway bus, about 9 to 10 h, $50 to $90; or Coast Starlight from Emeryville or San Jose, 11 to 12 h, $60 to $120+</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">6 to 7.5 h, $30 to $55 + 5% fee</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Los Angeles to San Diego</td><td class="win" data-l="Amtrak">Pacific Surfliner, direct, 2 h 45 to 3 h, $30 to $45</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">2 to 2.5 h, $15 to $30 + 5% fee</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sacramento to San Francisco</td><td class="win" data-l="Amtrak">Capitol Corridor to Emeryville plus bus, 2 to 2.5 h, $30 to $40</td><td data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">1.5 to 2 h, $15 to $25 + 5% fee</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Los Angeles to Santa Barbara</td><td data-l="Amtrak">Pacific Surfliner, 2 h 45, $30 to $40</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">1.5 to 2 h, $15 to $25 + 5% fee</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fresno to Los Angeles</td><td data-l="Amtrak">San Joaquins to Bakersfield plus Thruway bus, 4.5 to 5 h, $35 to $50</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">3.5 to 4 h, $25 to $40 + 5% fee</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Los Angeles to Las Vegas</td><td data-l="Amtrak">No Amtrak service</td><td class="win" data-l="Seat Sherpa seat">4.5 to 5.5 h, $25 to $55 + 5% fee</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>What the train does better</h2>
  <p>Space, a cafe car, power at every seat, and the freedom to work or sleep. The Coast Starlight south of San Luis Obispo is one of the best views in the state. Amtrak also carries bikes on most California trains and has a real luggage allowance. If you are not in a hurry and the corridor has a direct train, it is a comfortable choice.</p>

  <h2>What the carpool does better</h2>
  <p>Price and door-to-door time on the routes where the train needs a bus connection or does not run at all. Pickup is arranged in chat, so a Caltrain, BART or Metro station near you can be the meeting point instead of a downtown terminal. Payment is held by Stripe until the 4-digit pickup code confirms you are in the car.</p>

  <div class="callout" style="text-align:center">
    <h3>See live seat prices on your route</h3>
    <p style="margin-bottom:6px">Drivers post trips they are already taking. Book in the browser or the app; no account needed to look.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/rides?c=compare">Browse rides →</a>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:#8a8a92;margin-top:10px">Driving somewhere yourself? <a href="/post">Post the ride</a> and split the cost.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is there a direct Amtrak train from San Francisco to Los Angeles?</h3><p>No. The San Joaquins route requires a Thruway bus connection and takes about 9 to 10 hours, and the Coast Starlight from Emeryville or San Jose takes 11 to 12 hours. A Seat Sherpa carpool seat covers the route in 6 to 7.5 hours for $30 to $55 plus a 5% fee.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is the train or a carpool cheaper from LA to San Diego?</h3><p>The carpool is usually cheaper, typically $15 to $30 plus a 5% fee against $30 to $45 on the Pacific Surfliner, but the Surfliner is direct, frequent and comfortable, so both are good options on this corridor.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Does Amtrak go to Las Vegas?</h3><p>No. There has been no Amtrak service to Las Vegas since 1997. Options are the bus, flying, driving, or a carpool seat with Seat Sherpa on the Los Angeles to Las Vegas route.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>How much does a Seat Sherpa seat cost?</h3><p>It depends on the route and the driver, but every seat has a hard cap: the IRS standard mileage rate (about $0.76 per mile in 2026) multiplied by the drivable miles, divided across the seats, and never more than $55 a seat. Riders pay the seat price plus a 5% service fee, shown before you pay. Live prices for each corridor are on the route pages and in the ride browser.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>Is Seat Sherpa safe?</h3><p>Every driver verifies a phone number by SMS, uploads a driver’s license that is checked for expiry, registers the vehicle, and connects a Stripe account that verifies identity and bank details. Riders see the driver’s photo, trip count and reviews before booking, can filter for women drivers, and can block anyone. A 4-digit pickup code confirms the rider got in the car and is what releases payment.</p></div>
  <div class="faq"><h3>What is the cancellation policy?</h3><p>One standard policy on every ride: cancel 24 or more hours before departure for a full seat refund, 2 to 24 hours before for 50%, and inside 2 hours there is no refund. The 5% service fee is non-refundable when the rider cancels. If the driver cancels, the rider gets 100% back including the fee.</p></div>

